==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|exquisitus|exquīsītus|lang=la}}, perfect passive participle of {{term|exquiro|exquīrō|seek out|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-exquisite.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Especially [[fine]] or [[pleasing]]; [[exceptional]].
#: ''They sell good coffee and pastries, but their chocolate is '''exquisite'''.''
# {{obsolete}} Carefully adjusted; precise; accurate; exact.
# [[recherché|Recherché]]; [[far-fetched]]; [[abstruse]].
# Of special [[beauty]] or rare [[excellence]].

====Synonyms====
* [[beautiful]], [[delicate]], [[discriminating]]

